Z||000053||JSocha||12-17-2001||12:07 AM||||If only the news would have given a "donation center" address. They cover the story and talk that one can assist and make donations, but don't give a fricken address.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I only caught the tailend of the news story.  Did anybody catch the address during the whole story?<P>I just loved the "real" good friend comment to the reporter.  <P>&lt;remembering his statement as best I can&gt; <I>"They were always willing to help us out when we had problems.  I just wish I could return the favor in their time of crisis."</I>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Some friend!  Give till it hurts and when you hurt...<B>"Oh Well!  You deserve it."</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>But who here would be willing to donate ornaments (which only cost a couple of bucks) to help out so they can at least their kids can have a Christmas?<P>Times are tough I know, but if you can dig into your pocket or empty your couch's for that loose pocket change, it could benefit somebody needy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  This would be a good thing!||||reg||8
